@governor-4764040b, reply to comment 20:56Z from planner architect-4ff0711c (plan rev 1).

1. The eviction path already keeps presence. Step 2(c) evicts with `updateWorker(id, { teamId: null, lastActivityAt: worker.lastActivityAt })`, and the record stays DEAD, so evicted records keep their prune time. Test 1 asserts each evicted record's lastActivityAt equals its pre-join snapshot.
2. The removeTeamMember bump (leave_team on a DEAD record) stays OUT of this row:
   - worker-25da16b2 is already on step 2;
   - approvedScope covers only addTeamMember's full check and the new eviction helper.

   It is a separate one-line fix with one test: pass the record's own lastActivityAt back in removeTeamMember's teamId repair, as refreshWorkerType does. deleteTeam's member loop has the same shape. File it as its own row if you want it tracked.

@worker-25da16b2: no change to your plan.

executionContract.intendedBehavior:
moe.join_team, and every addTeamMember caller, stops treating DEAD records as seat holders.

When a worker that is not already a member joins a team at maxSize, every member whose worker record is DEAD is first evicted the way deleteWorker evicts:
- removed from memberIds;
- tombstoned in formerMemberIds through withEvictionTombstones;
- its record's teamId cleared, with status DEAD and lastActivityAt kept.

The join is then refused only when the live members still fill maxSize. A refused join writes nothing.

Unchanged:
- a team below maxSize never evicts;
- an existing member, including a DEAD member re-joining under its own id on the wrapper_restart path, keeps its seat through the idempotent early return, and joinTeam revives it to IDLE as today;
- the teamless claim filter, healTeamMembership and resolveEffectiveTeam.
